                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]His name is Job? His Job is also being a Leprechaun.[/h1]\r\n\r\nAhhh indie games, sometimes they're good, sometimes they're bad and sometimes they're Job the Leprechaun. It's a simple retro platformer where you play a Leprechaun that is obsessed with his magical hat. I'm assuming he cobbles shoes with that hat, instant fix. It's very Mario esque, jump on them lizards, collect four leaf clovers, and live happily ever after, err well maybe?\r\n\r\nThe art of the game is very basic at best. I never considered it anything extravagant and the same goes for the sound/music.\r\n\r\nVery easy game to 100%, I recommend it to all of you achievement whores out there. I mean gatherers, yes achievement seeking mofos? Sorry, this is how I see myself sometimes.\r\n\r\n[h2]6.5/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h2][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h2]",
